<title>USA: Sherwin-Williams may issue $700 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Sherwin-Williams may issue $700 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sherwin-Williams Co is expected to offer $700 million in multi-tranche corporate debt next week through a Salomon Brothers syndicate, sources said.</p>
<p>The deal will include $100 million each of three- and five-year debt and $200 million of 10-year debt in a public offering, sources said. Another $300 million will be sold through a private offering, they added.</p>
</text>
